          %h3#ClassesOnTotalSpace String structures by gerbes on a bundle
          %p One can reformulate an
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"}> orientation
                \-
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"}> Spin
                \-
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"}> String
                \-
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fivebrane+structure"}> Fivebrane
                \-
          %p
            structure in terms of the existence of a certain class in abelian cohomolgy on the total space of the given
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+principle+of+nonabelian+cohomology"} Whitehead principle of nonabelian cohomology
          #StringStrucDefinitionByTotalSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a manifolds with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi Spin
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S : X \to \mathbf{B}Spin
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
              for the corresponding
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            %p
              Then a
              %strong string structure
              lifting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a cohomology class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3(P,\mathbb{Z})
              such that the restriction of the class to any fiber
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq Spin(n)
              is a generator of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^3(Spin(n), \mathbb{Z}) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            This kind of definition appears in (
            %a{:href => "#Redden"}> Redden, def. 6.4.2
            ).
          #DirectStringStructureImpliesIndirectOne.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Every string structure in the sense of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FiberOverSpinStructure"}
              induces a string structure in the sense of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StringStrucDefinitionByTotalSpace"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting"} pasting
              diagram of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi String
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi P
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Spin
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
