          %h2#References References
          %p
            The relevance of String structures was originally recognized in the physics of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+strings"} spinning strings
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} super
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structures"} spin structures
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+particles"} spinning particles
            = succeed "." do
              %em string structure
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px -5px 30px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/Killingback-IntroducingStringStructure.jpg", :width => "400px"}/
          %p The coinage “string structure” is due to p. 585 (shown on the right) of:
          %ul
            %li#Killingback87
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Timothy+Killingback"}> Timothy Killingback
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em World-sheet anomalies and loop geometry
              %strong 288
              578-588 (1987) [
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(87)90229-X"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(87)90229-X
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/237516"} inSpire:237516
              = succeed "]" do
                %a{:href => "https://lib-extopc.kek.jp/preprints/PDF/1987/8704/8704177.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            where this structure is understood as a de-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            (both the naming and this insight are often incorrectly attributed to various mathematicians) of the required “spin structure on loop space”, due to
          %ul
            %li#WittenIndexLoopSpace
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Index of the Dirac Operator in Loop Space
                %em Elliptic Curves and Modular Forms in Algebraic Topology
                (Princeton, N.J., Sep 1986), Lecture Notes in Mathematics
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 1326
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0078045"} doi:10.1007/BFb0078045
            %li#WittenElliptic
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elliptic Genera and Quantum Field Theory
                %strong 109
                (1987) 525–536 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01208956"}> doi:10.1007/BF01208956
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            which arises as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomaly+cancellation"} anomaly cancellation
            condition on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            of the
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            = succeed "\u2019s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            may be understood (
            %a{:href => "spinning+particle#Witten85"}> Witten 1985
            ) as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomaly+cancellation"} anomaly cancellation
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldline"} worldline
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+particles"} spinning particles
            such as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superparticles"} superparticles
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              R. Coquereaux, K. Pilch:
              = succeed "," do
                %em String structures on loop bundles
              %strong 120
              (1989) 353–378 (1989) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01225503"}> doi:10.1007/BF01225503
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The understanding of Killingback’s string structure equivalently as the condition to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangential+structure"} lifting
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+group"} structure group
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            to a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+group"} string group
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephan+Stolz"}> Stephan Stolz
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Teichner"} Peter Teichner
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/What+is+an+elliptic+object%3F"} What is an elliptic object?
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topology, geometry and quantum field theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 308
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://math.berkeley.edu/~teichner/Papers/Oxford.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Stolz-Teichner_EllipticObject.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p The relation between the two pictures is further analyzed for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              A. Asada:
              %em Characteristic classes of loop group bundles and generalized string classes
              , Differential geometry and its applications (Eger, 1989), 33–66, Colloq. Math. Soc. János Bolyai, 56, North-Holland, Amsterdam, 1992. (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Asada.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A mathematically rigorous formulation of
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a{:href => "#Killingback87"} Killingback 1987
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em String structures and trivialisations of a Pfaffian line bundle
              %strong 307
              (2011) : 675-712 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0909.0846"}> arXiv:0909.0846
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-011-1348-0"} doi:10.1007/s00220-011-1348-0
          %p in turn reviewed in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"}> Konrad Waldorf
              ,
              %em Geometric string structure and supersymmetric sigma-models
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.konradwaldorf.de/docs/cardiff.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The definition of string structures by degree-3 classes on the total space of the spin bundle (also already mentioned by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Killingback87"} Killingback 1987
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Corbett+Redden"}> Corbett Redden
                ,
                %em Canonical metric connections associated to string structures
                PhD Thesis (2006) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.sunysb.edu/~redden/Thesis.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Redden &amp; Waldorf at
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oberwolfach+Workshop%2C+June+2009+--+Friday%2C+June+12"} Oberwolfach Workshop, June 2009 – Friday, June 12
          %p
            Discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+differential+string+structures"} twisted differential string structures
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Twisted+Differential+String+and+Fivebrane+Structures"} Twisted Differential String and Fivebrane Structures
              %strong 315
              1 (2012) 169-213 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.4001"}> arXiv:0910.4001
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-012-1510-3"} doi:10.1007/s00220-012-1510-3
          %p
            and its appearance on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            under
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Hypothesis+H"} Hypothesis H
          %ul
            %li#FSS21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Twisted+Cohomotopy+implies+twisted+String+structure+on+M5-branes"} Twisted Cohomotopy implies twisted String structure on M5-branes
              %strong 62
              (2021) 042301 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.11093"}> arXiv:2002.11093
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/5.0037786"} doi:10.1063/5.0037786
          %p
            An explicit cocycle construction of the essentially unique
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            lift of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} 5-sphere
            is given in
          %ul
            %li#Roberts14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Roberts"}> David Roberts
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Explicit string bundles
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://www.christiansaemann.de/higherworkshop2014/index.html"} Workshop on Higher Gauge Theory and Higher Quantization
              2014,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.04544"} arXiv:2203.04544
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/RobertsStringS5.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Discussion for indefinite (Lorentzian) signature is in
          %ul
            %li
              Hyung Bo Shim,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Indefinite string structure
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://d-scholarship.pitt.edu/19620/"} web
          %p More discussion of relation to spin structures on loop spaces is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Alessandra Capotosti,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/From+String+structures+to+Spin+structures+on+loop+spaces"} From String structures to Spin structures on loop spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"}> Konrad Waldorf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String structures and loop spaces
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Mathematical+Physics+2nd+ed"} Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics 2nd ed
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.12998"} arXiv:2312.12998
          %p A study of (flat) string structures encoded in the bicategory of flat 2-group bundles on an oriented surface via weak representations of the fundamental group is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Berwick-Evans"}> Daniel Berwick-Evans
              , Emily Cliff, Laura Murray, Apurva Nakade, Emma Phillips,
              %em String structures, 2-group bundles, and a categorification of the Freed-Quinn line bundle
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.07571"}> arXiv:2110.07571
              )
        .revisedby
